<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Mannaea</h1><p class="st-meta">850 BCE – 616 BCE (approx.) · capital Izirtu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Iron Age kingdom south of Lake Urmia, squeezed between Assyria and Urartu, that eventually merged into the Median state.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Mannaeans (Mannai) appear in Assyrian texts from the 840s BCE, inhabiting north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> around the southern shores of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-urmia">Lake Urmia</a>. By the late 8th century they had become a unified kingdom with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/izirtu">Izirtu</a> (Zirta), perhaps near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saqqez">Saqqez</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Mannaea was rich in horses and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and controlled routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-urartu">Urartu</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-plateau">Iranian plateau</a>. Its kings usually sided with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> against the Kingdom of Urartu: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranzu">Iranzu</a> was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II's</a> ally, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon</a> confirmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ullusunu">Ullusunu</a> on the throne after he abandoned an alliance with Urartu. Sites such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziwiye">Ziwiye</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qalaichi">Qalaichi</a>, with its stele and glazed bricks, may reflect Mannaean culture. Its language is unknown.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashurbanipal">Ashurbanipal</a> defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahsheri">Ahsheri</a> around 660 BCE. In 616 BCE Mannaean troops fought alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabopolassar">Nabopolassar</a>, but after Assyria's fall the kingdom was absorbed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/median-empire">Median Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/mannaea.jpg" alt="Mannaea" width="320" height="307"><figcaption>Image: Yak · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:UrmiaM2KP.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>850 BCE – 616 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Izirtu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Iranzu, Ullusunu, Ahsheri</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Iran</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mannai, Kingdom of the Mannaeans</dd></dl></aside></div>

